kylin-virtual-keyboard: keep the keyboard sized to the screen when the view is
preloaded (fixes "rotate while hidden, then open -> stale size")

STATUS: this is an UPSTREAM-GRADE fix, not a required step for sheng images.
sheng already works around the bug at runtime with the sheng-osk-rotate daemon
(install_osk_tap step 5: when the orientation changed while the keyboard was
hidden, restart the keyboard process so the view is rebuilt at the current
orientation).  Apply this patch only if you are rebuilding the keyboard -- e.g.
to hand it to openKylin upstream, or to drop the daemon afterwards
(build with OSK_ROTATE_ENV=0 while keeping OSK_PRELOAD_ENV=1).

sheng/openKylin 3.0 regression analysis (device 192.168.5.15, 2026-10-09).

Symptom
-------
With gsettings org.ukui.virtualkeyboard preload-view-enabled=true:
  * rotate the screen while the keyboard is OPEN  -> it resizes correctly
  * hide the keyboard, rotate, then open it again -> the keyboard keeps the
    size of whatever orientation was active when its view was created
With preload-view-enabled=false (the upstream default) both work, because the
view is destroyed on hide and rebuilt on show, and initView() applies a fresh
geometry every time.

Root cause
----------
The geometry is computed live on every call:
  geometrymanager.cpp:54        geometry() -> QRect(calculateViewPosition(), calculateViewSize())
  expansiongeometrymanager.cpp:24  calculateViewWidth() -> ScreenWatcher::getOptimalScreenGeometry(...).width()
  screenwatcher.cpp:39          getOptimalScreenGeometry() -> QScreen::geometry()
and the rotation event itself is emitted correctly:
  screenwatcher.cpp:241         if (screenMarked) emit screensChanged();

but the *application* of that geometry to the window is gated on visibility:
  virtualkeyboardmanager.cpp:274  if (!view_->isVisible()) return;   // handleScreensChanged
  virtualkeyboardview.cpp:102     if (!isVisible()) return;         // updateGeometry()

so rotating while the keyboard is hidden does nothing.  The one place that
applies a fresh geometry unconditionally is initView():
  virtualkeyboardview.cpp:196     view_->setGeometry(calculateInitialGeometry());

and with preload enabled initView() bails out early on every later show:
  virtualkeyboardview.cpp:150     if (view_ != nullptr && preloadViewEnabled) return;

Result: the window size stays frozen at view-creation time (= the orientation at
login, since preload builds the view at startup).

Fix
---
When initView() reuses a preloaded view, re-apply the geometry if the size the
current screen implies differs from the window's.  Comparing the size (rather
than always re-applying) preserves the original show animation: on the first
show after startup nothing changes, so the window keeps the off-screen y from
calculateInitialGeometry() and slides in as before.  Upstream may prefer
tracking this with an explicit "geometry invalidated while hidden" flag.

Verified by code inspection against the sources shipped on the device
(/home/luser/kvk, virtualkeyboardview.cpp md5 43510c5ec4513c112ad225724b09c42f).
Not compile-tested: the device has no qtbase5-dev/qtdeclarative5-dev, so the
keyboard cannot be rebuilt there -- build it where the full tree is available.

--- a/src/virtualkeyboard/virtualkeyboardview.cpp
+++ b/src/virtualkeyboard/virtualkeyboardview.cpp
@@ -147,7 +147,20 @@
 void VirtualKeyboardView::initView() {
     const auto preloadViewEnabled =
         VirtualKeyboardSettings::getInstance().isPreloadViewEnabled();
     if (view_ != nullptr && preloadViewEnabled) {
+        // sheng: the view is reused, so it also keeps the window size it was
+        // created with.  handleScreensChanged()/updateGeometry() deliberately
+        // do nothing while the keyboard is hidden, so a rotation that happened
+        // while it was hidden leaves the window at the old size and the next
+        // show() would present a stale one.  Re-apply the geometry when the
+        // current screen implies a different size.  Comparing the size (instead
+        // of always re-applying) keeps the original show animation: right after
+        // startup the size is unchanged, so the off-screen y from
+        // calculateInitialGeometry() survives and the keyboard still slides in.
+        const QRect currentGeometry = geometry();
+        if (view_->size() != currentGeometry.size()) {
+            view_->setGeometry(currentGeometry);
+        }
         return;
     }
     KVKBD_INFO("preloadViewEnabled:{}", preloadViewEnabled);
